# provenance: 81dd26a — the guest's RLE apply cleared only the TAIL, so a zero
# run in the middle of a region left the old liquid in place and the guest's
# fluid grew without bound ("the guest's water is visibly more"). The region is
# an ABSOLUTE snapshot of its rectangle (FluidRleCodec.Decode): EVERY cell is
# written, zero runs included; the uncovered tail is cleared. The first region
# carries the exact bug shape — a mid-region zero run ([10,2, 0,1, 20,1] over
# 4 cells) — and the replay asserts the guest's applied grid, which runs the
# real decoder: a decode regression breaks this file instead of silently
# replaying the old bug. The overwrite and partial-clear steps lock the
# absolute-overwrite semantics (an uncovered cell keeps its value).
# Mechanism: FluidRegionMsg (NetMsg 70, unreliable), FluidRleCodec.cs.
@0 fluid g1 0 0 4 1 10 2 0 1 20 1
@33 expect fluid g1 0 0 10 within 500
@33 expect fluid g1 1 0 10 within 500
@33 expect fluid g1 2 0 0 within 500
@33 expect fluid g1 3 0 20 within 500
@33 fluid g1 0 0 4 1 5 4
@66 expect fluid g1 0 0 5 within 500
@66 expect fluid g1 3 0 5 within 500
@66 fluid g1 0 0 2 1 0 2
@99 expect fluid g1 0 0 0 within 500
@99 expect fluid g1 1 0 0 within 500
@99 expect fluid g1 2 0 5 within 500
@99 expect fluid g1 3 0 5 within 500
